# L §2.4 Values, §8.3 LOAD-KEY (tally 2.1.7 R9, issue #148; #100a): a month a key-typed input's row names
# prints as a month, `2031-05`. 2.1.6's refcore printed the tuple `(2031, 5)`. (T's code vector written/key-month.)
=== base.tally
model written
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T's base for M0's load-code fixtures (invented, issue #90): keys and a price written in rows and clauses; a place keyed by persons, an observation's leg to one of them, an input keyed by a stepped range, a priced holding; it loads clean; each fixture of codes/m0/edits.tsv changes one line"

source card "T's fixture card (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

unit etf_unit "a fund unit"

kind persons

kind gifts: event certain
  leg cash: PLN

place konto[p in persons]: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place fund: holdings etf_unit priced fund_price lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

input bank: observed

input fund_price[m in months]: num PLN/etf_unit

input rr[k in 1..9 step 2]: money PLN

input amt: money PLN

input who: key months

ask q: amt + rr[3]

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ana] lives 2026-01-01..
  persons + [ben] lives 2026-01-01..
  amt = 1.00 PLN "the card"
  rr[3] = 2.00 PLN "the card"
  who = 2031-05 "the card"
  opening[konto[ana]] = 1.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "the card"
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-02-01, kind: gifts, leg cash from world to konto[ana] amount 1.00 PLN) "a gift"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-KEY 2031-05 is not a key of months ...
